    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) & Smith et al. (2006) up-the-gradient PIN1 polarization with explicit PIN1 trafficking kinetics, quasi-3D subepidermal canalization, and polar auxin transport for shoot apical meristem phyllotaxis (Arabidopsis thaliana (shoot apical meristem L1 epidermis & subepidermal provascular strand); Aeonium tabuliforme (spiral rosette specimen))" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-5> ;
    schema:about "Arabidopsis thaliana (shoot apical meristem L1 epidermis & subepidermal provascular strand); Aeonium tabuliforme (spiral rosette specimen)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Full 3D meristem geometry, tissue growth or cell division, PIN1 phosphorylation (PINOID/PP2A) control of apical-basal targeting, emergent golden-angle phyllotaxis, emergent mode transitions with Gamma, or a quantitative comparison of PIN1 plasma-membrane fractions with immunolocalization data",
        "reconstructed_in_script: ExG + DoG segmentation of 410 leaf tips on the SHA-256-locked Aeonium tabuliforme rosette (12/12 sectors, NN 1 - CV = 0.774)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Explicit per-cell cytosolic + per-wall membrane PIN1 pools cycling by first-order exocytosis (targeting f_ij = exp(c_1 (a_j - a_0))) and endocytosis, solved by an exact exponential integrator (membrane + cytosol conservation err 0.0, flux antisymmetry err 1.3e-14), with QSS ablation, BFA block (PM fraction 0.0857 after 2 h = PM(t_BFA) exp(-k_endo 2 h) exactly; polarity 0.052 vs WT 0.584), auxin-inhibited-endocytosis variant (polarity 0.21) and fast-cycling Boltzmann limit (max |P - Boltzmann| 0.013)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Linearized Turing-like dispersion relation with kappa_4 calibrated so that the peak sits at the 5.2-cell reference (threshold c_1 a_0 = 1.75; NPA collapse sigma(k) < 0); 1D ring NPA (contrast 1.000, 0 peaks) and IAA-paste rescue (1 peak at 60 deg)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Quasi-3D 15 x 12 subepidermal slice beneath P1 with with-the-flux Hill feedback f_ij = f_0 + J^n/(K^n + J^n): single-file strand (width 1 cell at mid-depth, mean 1.0 over rows 1-8, flux concentration 0.63, 97 % of source flux delivered to the sink); no-feedback ablation width 14 cells; Hill-exponent sweep widths {15, 6, 1, 1, 1} for n in {1, 1.5, 2, 2.5, 3} (Spearman rho -0.89, p 0.04)",
        "reported_in_source: Bayer et al. (2009) Genes Dev: epidermal up-the-gradient patterning couples to subepidermal with-the-flux canalization (Mitchison 1980/1981; Feugier et al. 2005) producing a narrow provascular strand from the L1 convergence point to the existing vasculature; Scarpella et al. (2006): PIN1-marked preprocambial strands are 1-2 cells wide",
        "reported_in_source: Geldner et al. (2001) Nature: brefeldin A blocks PIN1 exocytosis and internalises plasma-membrane PIN1 within 1-2 h; Paciorek et al. (2005) Nature: auxin inhibits PIN endocytosis",
        "reported_in_source: Jönsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103:1633-1638 & Smith et al. (2006) PNAS 103:1301-1306: up-the-gradient PIN1 membrane allocation P_ij = P_i exp(c_1 a_j) / sum_k exp(c_1 a_k) with explicit PIN1 membrane cycling kinetics whose quasi-steady state is that allocation, intercellular active polar + diffusive auxin transport, and periodic convergence maxima separated by a characteristic wavelength",
        "reported_in_source: Smith et al. (2006): transitions across spiral (137.5 deg), distichous (180 deg), decussate (90 deg) and tricussate (120 deg) phyllotaxis with meristem size; Reinhardt et al. (2003) Nature: NPA/pin1 pin-formed apex and localized IAA rescue",
        "transfer_boundary: The 180-cell dome does NOT generate its primordia: P1..P8 are seeded at golden-angle targets (L396-397) and the auxin field is relaxed toward a prescribed envelope (L508-513); only the PIN1 trafficking, polarity, conservation and BFA/QSS/fast-cycling results are emergent outputs of that function",
        "transfer_boundary: The canalization model is one non-growing vertical slice with a uniform Dirichlet sink row, no lateral neighbours' strands, no growth and no 3D geometry; strand width is compared to a literature band (1-2 cells), not to a vendored PIN1::GFP image",
        "transfer_boundary: The four phyllotactic regimes are prescribed (nominal angle + seeded noise, L944-957; spiral placed at k*137.5 deg, L923-931) and the WT ring profile is hand-built (L1025-1028); Gamma is a label, not a control parameter",
        "transfer_boundary: The rosette specimen is Aeonium tabuliforme (top-down leaf rosette), not an Arabidopsis inflorescence meristem" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Auxin flux vein / phyllotactic primordium in Arabidopsis thaliana" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "4. Polar Auxin & Turgor Stress" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Spirals, Veins & Puzzle Cells" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Golden Angle / Auxin Flux" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Arabidopsis" ;
