<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) & Smith et al. (2006) up-the-gradient PIN1 polarization with explicit PIN1 trafficking kinetics, quasi-3D subepidermal canalization, and polar auxin transport for shoot apical meristem phyllotaxis — Code-to-model traceability: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the module docstring maps Laws 1-5 to Jönsson Eqs. 1-4, Smith Eq. 2, Reinhardt Figs. 1-2, Geldner 2001, Paciorek 2005, Mitchison 1980/1981, Feugier 2005 and Bayer 2009, and to the five Lean theorems with line loci (L1-66); every Pass 3 function docstring states its equations and which paper step it reduces (L238-262, L309-347, L617-651, L773-779, L820-836); the math KG YAML registers Laws 4-5 with code loci that match the current file. Deductions: the dome scaffolding constants (pz centre 33 um / width 11.5, envelope 1.35/0.55/2.65, weights 0.14 and 0.38, corona 3.5-11.5 um) are uncited (L407-415, L508-513, L543-549) (-8); the canalization constants f_0 = 0.1, K = 1.0, T_periclinal = 0.3 and a_sink = 0.2 are model choices documented in the JSON but not derived from any paper (-5); kappa_4 is described as 'calibrated' without stating that this makes lambda_c an input (-3); the Panel E/C titles were only relabelled in Pass 3 and still display prescribed values (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py L404–L415: pz_profile / prim_envelope constants (33, 11.5, 4.6, 0.055, 0.15, 0.35) carry no citation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L404-L415>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) & Smith et al. (2006) up-the-gradient PIN1 polarization with explicit PIN1 trafficking kinetics, quasi-3D subepidermal canalization, and polar auxin transport for shoot apical meristem phyllotaxis — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the Boltzmann allocation and antisymmetric active + diffusive flux (L434-439, L495-499) match Jönsson Eqs. 1-4 / Smith Eq. 2; the new trafficking kinetics dP_ij/dt = k_exo f P_cyt - k_endo P_ij with pool conservation are the paper's PIN1 cycling scheme and are solved exactly (L238-284), with the QSS, BFA (k_exo = 0) and fast-cycling limits all behaving as Law 4 predicts (L820-886); the canalization slice implements the Mitchison/Feugier with-the-flux rule with the same trafficking kinetics (L705-716) and reproduces winner-take-all strand formation (Law 5). Deductions: the dome's auxin equation is not Jönsson Eq. 1 — the transport term is down-weighted by 0.14 and the field is relaxed at rate 0.38 toward a hand-built envelope target_a = 1.35 + 0.55 pz + 2.65 prim (L508-513), with the primordia seeded at golden-angle targets (L396-397), so the convergence maxima are imposed (-10); the four phyllotactic regimes are not simulated at all — nominal angle plus seeded noise (L944-957) and golden placement by construction (L923-931) (-8); the WT ring profile is a sum of five hand-placed Gaussians (L1025-1028) (-3); kappa_4 is calibrated so the dispersion peak hits the 5.2-cell reference (L180-184), so lambda_c is an input (-3); the canalization is a single non-growing slice with a uniform sink row rather than the requested 3D tissue (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py L180–L184: kappa_4 = alpha_eff / s*(5.2 cells): the dispersion peak is calibrated to the reference it is later compared against <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L180-L184>",
        "2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py L396–L415: P1..P8 seeded at (k+1)*golden + N(0, 0.012 rad) and the initial auxin field pre-shaped by prim_envelope: primordium positions are inputs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L396-L415>",
        "2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py L506–L514: da/dt = rho0 - mu a + 0.14 sum J + 0.38 (target_a - a): a relaxation toward a prescribed envelope, not Jönsson Eq. 1 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L506-L514>",
        "2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py L921–L960: Four 'regimes': spiral placed at k*137.5 deg by construction; distichous/decussate/tricussate = nominal angle + seeded noise; Gamma unused in the dynamics <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L921-L960>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) & Smith et al. (2006) up-the-gradient PIN1 polarization with explicit PIN1 trafficking kinetics, quasi-3D subepidermal canalization, and polar auxin transport for shoot apical meristem phyllotaxis — Morphometric validation: 68/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: 16 measurements with units, reference values, sources and methods (L1529-1680); the new ones compare against literature or against the paper's own analytic predictions rather than against themselves — strand width 1 cell vs the Scarpella/Bayer 1-2 cell band, delivered fraction 0.97 vs idealised 1.0 with the ablation at 0.68, BFA PM fraction 0.0857 equal to the first-order prediction (an identity for the exact integrator), kinetic-vs-QSS deviation 0.053 with the fast-cycling check 0.013, Spearman -0.89 for the exponent sweep; measurements #1 and #5 now say NOT EMERGENT in their method strings and #4 reports the raw cosine (0.994) instead of a value recalibrated onto the 0.84 reference. Deductions: #1 (L1549-1557, 137.39 deg) and #5 (L1581-1588, Pearson r = 1.0) remain in the list although they validate seeded inputs (-10); #4's 0.84 reference, the 2.68/2.85 contrasts and the per-regime Gamma values in the reference JSON are not traceable to a figure or table of the cited papers (-7); #12 (BFA) and #13 (endocytosis ratio) use model-derived references, so they are consistency checks rather than empirical comparisons (-5); the PM fraction reference 0.9 is a qualitative band edge, and no quantitative PIN1 localisation or strand-width measurement from an image is made (-6); #2 compares a calibrated peak to its calibration target (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py L1549–L1557: Measurement #1 method string: 'NOT EMERGENT: P1..P8 are seeded at golden-angle targets' <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L1549-L1557>",
        "2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py L1638–L1646: BFA measurement's reference_value is the model's own first-order prediction (self-consistency, not an empirical value) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L1638-L1646>",
        "datasets/auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis/auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis_reference.json L165–L189: perturbation_experiments contrasts 2.68 / 2.85 and convergence index 0.84 carry no figure/table pinpoint <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/datasets/auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis/auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis_reference.json#L165-L189>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-measurement-auxin-inhibited-endocytosis-polarity-ratio-vs-exocytosis-targeting>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-measurement-bfa-exocytosis-block-membrane-pin1-fraction-2h>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-measurement-canalization-flux-delivered-to-vascular-sink-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-measurement-canalization-strand-width-vs-feedback-exponent-spearman-rho>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-measurement-characteristic-primordium-spacing-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-measurement-critical-pin1-feedback-threshold-c1-a0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-measurement-exogenous-iaa-paste-rescue-peak-angle>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-measurement-four-mode-divergence-angle-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-measurement-npa-polar-transport-block-contrast>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-measurement-pin1-plasma-membrane-fraction-wild-type>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-measurement-pin1-primordium-convergence-polarity-index>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-measurement-pin1-trafficking-kinetic-vs-analytic-qss-max-abs-deviation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-measurement-specimen-rosette-azimuthal-sector-coverage>,
