<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) & Smith et al. (2006) Up-the-Gradient Boltzmann PIN1 Allocation Law" ;
    dct:description "Directs cellular PIN1 efflux carriers preferentially toward neighboring cells with higher auxin concentration while conserving each cell's total PIN1 pool | Variables: P_i: total PIN1 pool in L1 cell i; P_ij: PIN1 allocated to anticlinal wall i→j; a_j: auxin concentration in neighbor cell j; c_1: up-the-gradient feedback exponent; w_j = exp(c_1 a_j): Boltzmann weight" ;
    dct:source "Jönsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1633-1638 Eq. 4; Smith et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1301-1306 Eq. 2" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L134-L224>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_032_auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis.lean#L27-L44> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def pin1_alloc_scaled (P_i w_j : Int) : Int := P_i * w_j
def pin1_partition_sum3 (w1 w2 w3 : Int) : Int := w1 + w2 + w3
theorem jonsson_2006_up_gradient_pin1_allocation (P_i w1 w2 w3 w_j w_k : Int)
    (hP : P_i > 0) (hw : w_j > w_k) :
    pin1_alloc_scaled P_i w1 + pin1_alloc_scaled P_i w2 + pin1_alloc_scaled P_i w3 =
      P_i * pin1_partition_sum3 w1 w2 w3 ∧
    pin1_alloc_scaled P_i w_j > pin1_alloc_scaled P_i w_k
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_ij = P_i exp(c_1 a_j) / ∑_{k∈N(i)} exp(c_1 a_k);  ∑_{j∈N(i)} P_ij = P_i;  a_j > a_k ⇒ P_ij > P_ik" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2005.09.052>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/35096571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03633>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0015>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0154>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.497009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Up-the-Gradient Auxin-PIN1 Polarized Transport & Turing-Like Phyllotactic Spacing" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.pin1_alloc_scaled" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.jonsson_2006_up_gradient_pin1_allocation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) Intercellular Active Polar + Diffusive Auxin Flux Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Guarantees exact pairwise intercellular auxin mass conservation across every shared cell wall and equilibrium stationarity at homogeneous state a_0 = ρ_0 / μ | Variables: a_i: auxin concentration in cell i; T: active PIN1 polar transport rate; D: passive apoplastic/plasmodesmatal diffusion rate; ρ_0: basal auxin synthesis rate; μ: auxin turnover rate" ;
    dct:source "Jönsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1633-1638 Eqs. 1-3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L309-L615>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_032_auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis.lean#L59-L71> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def intercellular_auxin_flux (T D P_ij P_ji a_i a_j : Int) : Int :=
  T * (P_ji * a_j - P_ij * a_i) + D * (a_j - a_i)
theorem jonsson_2006_intercellular_flux_conservation (T D P_ij P_ji P0 a_i a_j a0 : Int) :
    intercellular_auxin_flux T D P_ij P_ji a_i a_j +
      intercellular_auxin_flux T D P_ji P_ij a_j a_i = 0 ∧
    intercellular_auxin_flux T D P0 P0 a0 a0 = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "da_i/dt = ρ_0 - μ a_i + ∑_{j∈N(i)} J_{i←j},  J_{i←j} = T(P_ji a_j - P_ij a_i) + D(a_j - a_i),  J_{i←j} + J_{j←i} = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2005.09.052>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/35096571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03633>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0015>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0154>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.497009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Up-the-Gradient Auxin-PIN1 Polarized Transport & Turing-Like Phyllotactic Spacing" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.intercellular_auxin_flux" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.jonsson_2006_intercellular_flux_conservation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) Up-the-Gradient Turing-Like Instability & NPA Pin-Formed Collapse Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes the bifurcation threshold where up-the-gradient active transport overcomes passive diffusion to form periodic auxin convergence maxima separated by λ_c, and proves that blocking polar transport (T = 0 in NPA or pin1 mutant) abolishes instability to yield a pin-formed apex | Variables: c_1 a_0: dimensionless PIN1 polarization feedback product; z: cellular coordination number; D_eff: effective linearized diffusion coefficient; Γ_mode: spatial perturbation growth gain" ;
    dct:source "Jönsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1633-1638 pp. 1635-1636; Reinhardt et al. (2003) Nature 426:255-260" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L134-L224>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_032_auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis.lean#L90-L109> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def effective_diffusion_scaled (z_D T P_i c1_a0 : Int) : Int :=
  z_D - T * P_i * (c1_a0 - 1)
def mode_instability_gain (z_D T P_i c1_a0 : Int) : Int :=
  T * P_i * (c1_a0 - 1) - z_D
theorem jonsson_2006_up_gradient_instability_and_npa_collapse (z_D T P_i c1_a0 : Int)
    (h_instab : T * P_i * (c1_a0 - 1) > z_D)
    (h_diff : z_D > 0) :
    effective_diffusion_scaled z_D T P_i c1_a0 < 0 ∧
    mode_instability_gain z_D T P_i c1_a0 > 0 ∧
    mode_instability_gain z_D 0 P_i c1_a0 < 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Γ_mode = T P_i (c_1 a_0 - 1) - z D > 0  ⇔  D_eff < 0;  T = 0 (NPA / pin1) ⇒ Γ_mode = -z D < 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2005.09.052>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/35096571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03633>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0015>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0154>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.497009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Up-the-Gradient Auxin-PIN1 Polarized Transport & Turing-Like Phyllotactic Spacing" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.mode_instability_gain" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.jonsson_2006_up_gradient_instability_and_npa_collapse" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) Explicit PIN1 Exocytosis / Endocytosis Trafficking Kinetics & Quasi-Steady-State Allocation Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Replaces the instantaneous Boltzmann allocation by explicit membrane cycling with a finite trafficking time 1/k_endo; its fixed point conserves membrane + cytosolic PIN1, retains up-the-gradient polarity, reduces to Law 1 as k_endo/(k_exo ∑ f) → 0, and predicts complete PIN1 internalisation under a brefeldin A exocytosis block | Variables: P_cyt,i: cytosolic/endosomal PIN1 pool of cell i; P_ij: plasma-membrane PIN1 on wall i→j; k_exo: exocytosis rate per unit targeting weight; k_endo: endocytosis rate; f(a_j) = exp(c_1 (a_j − a_0)): up-the-gradient exocytosis targeting; Z_i: cleared partition denominator" ;
    dct:source "Jönsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1633-1638 (PIN1 cycling kinetics and quasi-steady state); Geldner et al. (2001) Nature 413:425-428 (BFA); Paciorek et al. (2005) Nature 435:1251-1256 (auxin-inhibited endocytosis)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L229-L306>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_032_auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis.lean#L136-L163> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def pin1_membrane_qss_num (k_exo f_j P_tot : Int) : Int := k_exo * f_j * P_tot
def pin1_cytosol_qss_num (k_endo P_tot : Int) : Int := k_endo * P_tot
def pin1_trafficking_partition (k_exo k_endo f1 f2 f3 : Int) : Int := k_endo + k_exo * (f1 + f2 + f3)
theorem jonsson_2006_pin1_trafficking_qss (k_exo k_endo f1 f2 f3 f_j f_k P_tot : Int)
    (hk : k_exo > 0) (hP : P_tot > 0) (hf : f_j > f_k) :
    pin1_cytosol_qss_num k_endo P_tot + pin1_membrane_qss_num k_exo f1 P_tot +
        pin1_membrane_qss_num k_exo f2 P_tot + pin1_membrane_qss_num k_exo f3 P_tot =
      P_tot * pin1_trafficking_partition k_exo k_endo f1 f2 f3 ∧
    k_endo * pin1_membrane_qss_num k_exo f_j P_tot =
      k_exo * f_j * pin1_cytosol_qss_num k_endo P_tot ∧
    pin1_membrane_qss_num k_exo f_j P_tot > pin1_membrane_qss_num k_exo f_k P_tot ∧
    pin1_membrane_qss_num 0 f_j P_tot = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "dP_ij/dt = k_exo f(a_j) P_cyt,i − k_endo P_ij,  P_cyt,i + ∑_j P_ij = P_tot;  P*_ij = k_exo f_j P_tot / Z_i,  P*_cyt = k_endo P_tot / Z_i,  Z_i = k_endo + k_exo ∑_k f_k;  k_endo P*_ij = k_exo f_j P*_cyt;  f_j > f_k ⇒ P*_ij > P*_ik;  k_exo = 0 (BFA) ⇒ P*_ij = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2005.09.052>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/35096571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03633>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0015>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0154>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.497009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Up-the-Gradient Auxin-PIN1 Polarized Transport & Turing-Like Phyllotactic Spacing" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.pin1_membrane_qss_num" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.jonsson_2006_pin1_trafficking_qss" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980/1981) With-the-Flux Canalization Winner-Take-All Law (subepidermal provascular strand; Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Shows that a superlinear flux feedback amplifies any flux asymmetry between competing walls, so a symmetric split is linearly unstable and auxin efflux canalizes into a single-file provascular strand connecting the L1 convergence point to the existing vasculature (Bayer et al. 2009 integration) | Variables: J_1, J_2: net auxin efflux through two competing walls of a subepidermal cell; Φ: with-the-flux exocytosis targeting (quadratic case of Φ = J^n/(K^n + J^n)); α: feedback gain (k_exo P_cyt)" ;
    dct:source "Mitchison GJ (1980) Proc. R. Soc. Lond. B 207:79-109; Mitchison GJ (1981) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. Lond. B 295:461-471; Feugier et al. (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:366-375; Bayer et al. (2009) Genes Dev. 23:373-384" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L617-L770>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_032_auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis.lean#L183-L202> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def flux_feedback_quadratic (J : Int) : Int := J * J
theorem mitchison_1980_canalization_winner_take_all (J1 J2 alpha : Int)
    (h2 : J2 ≥ 0) (h : J1 > J2) (ha : alpha > 0) :
    flux_feedback_quadratic J1 - flux_feedback_quadratic J2 = (J1 - J2) * (J1 + J2) ∧
    flux_feedback_quadratic J1 > flux_feedback_quadratic J2 ∧
    alpha * (flux_feedback_quadratic J1 - flux_feedback_quadratic J2) > 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Φ(J) = J²;  J_1 > J_2 ≥ 0 ⇒ Φ(J_1) − Φ(J_2) = (J_1 − J_2)(J_1 + J_2) > 0;  α > 0 ⇒ α (Φ(J_1) − Φ(J_2)) > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2005.09.052>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/35096571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03633>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0015>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0154>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.497009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Up-the-Gradient Auxin-PIN1 Polarized Transport & Turing-Like Phyllotactic Spacing" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.flux_feedback_quadratic" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.mitchison_1980_canalization_winner_take_all" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) & Smith et al. (2006) Up-the-Gradient Boltzmann PIN1 Allocation Law" ;
    dct:description "Directs cellular PIN1 efflux carriers preferentially toward neighboring cells with higher auxin concentration while conserving each cell's total PIN1 pool | Variables: P_i: total PIN1 pool in L1 cell i; P_ij: PIN1 allocated to anticlinal wall i→j; a_j: auxin concentration in neighbor cell j; c_1: up-the-gradient feedback exponent; w_j = exp(c_1 a_j): Boltzmann weight" ;
    dct:source "Jönsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1633-1638 Eq. 4; Smith et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1301-1306 Eq. 2" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L134-L224>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_032_auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis.lean#L27-L44> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def pin1_alloc_scaled (P_i w_j : Int) : Int := P_i * w_j
def pin1_partition_sum3 (w1 w2 w3 : Int) : Int := w1 + w2 + w3
theorem jonsson_2006_up_gradient_pin1_allocation (P_i w1 w2 w3 w_j w_k : Int)
    (hP : P_i > 0) (hw : w_j > w_k) :
    pin1_alloc_scaled P_i w1 + pin1_alloc_scaled P_i w2 + pin1_alloc_scaled P_i w3 =
      P_i * pin1_partition_sum3 w1 w2 w3 ∧
    pin1_alloc_scaled P_i w_j > pin1_alloc_scaled P_i w_k
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_ij = P_i exp(c_1 a_j) / ∑_{k∈N(i)} exp(c_1 a_k);  ∑_{j∈N(i)} P_ij = P_i;  a_j > a_k ⇒ P_ij > P_ik" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2005.09.052>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/35096571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03633>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0015>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0154>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.497009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Up-the-Gradient Auxin-PIN1 Polarized Transport & Turing-Like Phyllotactic Spacing" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.pin1_alloc_scaled" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.jonsson_2006_up_gradient_pin1_allocation" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) Intercellular Active Polar + Diffusive Auxin Flux Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Guarantees exact pairwise intercellular auxin mass conservation across every shared cell wall and equilibrium stationarity at homogeneous state a_0 = ρ_0 / μ | Variables: a_i: auxin concentration in cell i; T: active PIN1 polar transport rate; D: passive apoplastic/plasmodesmatal diffusion rate; ρ_0: basal auxin synthesis rate; μ: auxin turnover rate" ;
    dct:source "Jönsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1633-1638 Eqs. 1-3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L309-L615>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_032_auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis.lean#L59-L71> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def intercellular_auxin_flux (T D P_ij P_ji a_i a_j : Int) : Int :=
  T * (P_ji * a_j - P_ij * a_i) + D * (a_j - a_i)
theorem jonsson_2006_intercellular_flux_conservation (T D P_ij P_ji P0 a_i a_j a0 : Int) :
    intercellular_auxin_flux T D P_ij P_ji a_i a_j +
      intercellular_auxin_flux T D P_ji P_ij a_j a_i = 0 ∧
    intercellular_auxin_flux T D P0 P0 a0 a0 = 0
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "da_i/dt = ρ_0 - μ a_i + ∑_{j∈N(i)} J_{i←j},  J_{i←j} = T(P_ji a_j - P_ij a_i) + D(a_j - a_i),  J_{i←j} + J_{j←i} = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2005.09.052>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/35096571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03633>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0015>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0154>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.497009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Up-the-Gradient Auxin-PIN1 Polarized Transport & Turing-Like Phyllotactic Spacing" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.intercellular_auxin_flux" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.jonsson_2006_intercellular_flux_conservation" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) Up-the-Gradient Turing-Like Instability & NPA Pin-Formed Collapse Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes the bifurcation threshold where up-the-gradient active transport overcomes passive diffusion to form periodic auxin convergence maxima separated by λ_c, and proves that blocking polar transport (T = 0 in NPA or pin1 mutant) abolishes instability to yield a pin-formed apex | Variables: c_1 a_0: dimensionless PIN1 polarization feedback product; z: cellular coordination number; D_eff: effective linearized diffusion coefficient; Γ_mode: spatial perturbation growth gain" ;
    dct:source "Jönsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1633-1638 pp. 1635-1636; Reinhardt et al. (2003) Nature 426:255-260" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L134-L224>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_032_auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis.lean#L90-L109> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def effective_diffusion_scaled (z_D T P_i c1_a0 : Int) : Int :=
  z_D - T * P_i * (c1_a0 - 1)
def mode_instability_gain (z_D T P_i c1_a0 : Int) : Int :=
  T * P_i * (c1_a0 - 1) - z_D
theorem jonsson_2006_up_gradient_instability_and_npa_collapse (z_D T P_i c1_a0 : Int)
    (h_instab : T * P_i * (c1_a0 - 1) > z_D)
    (h_diff : z_D > 0) :
    effective_diffusion_scaled z_D T P_i c1_a0 < 0 ∧
    mode_instability_gain z_D T P_i c1_a0 > 0 ∧
    mode_instability_gain z_D 0 P_i c1_a0 < 0
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Γ_mode = T P_i (c_1 a_0 - 1) - z D > 0  ⇔  D_eff < 0;  T = 0 (NPA / pin1) ⇒ Γ_mode = -z D < 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2005.09.052>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/35096571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03633>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0015>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0154>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.497009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Up-the-Gradient Auxin-PIN1 Polarized Transport & Turing-Like Phyllotactic Spacing" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.mode_instability_gain" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.jonsson_2006_up_gradient_instability_and_npa_collapse" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) Explicit PIN1 Exocytosis / Endocytosis Trafficking Kinetics & Quasi-Steady-State Allocation Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Replaces the instantaneous Boltzmann allocation by explicit membrane cycling with a finite trafficking time 1/k_endo; its fixed point conserves membrane + cytosolic PIN1, retains up-the-gradient polarity, reduces to Law 1 as k_endo/(k_exo ∑ f) → 0, and predicts complete PIN1 internalisation under a brefeldin A exocytosis block | Variables: P_cyt,i: cytosolic/endosomal PIN1 pool of cell i; P_ij: plasma-membrane PIN1 on wall i→j; k_exo: exocytosis rate per unit targeting weight; k_endo: endocytosis rate; f(a_j) = exp(c_1 (a_j − a_0)): up-the-gradient exocytosis targeting; Z_i: cleared partition denominator" ;
    dct:source "Jönsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1633-1638 (PIN1 cycling kinetics and quasi-steady state); Geldner et al. (2001) Nature 413:425-428 (BFA); Paciorek et al. (2005) Nature 435:1251-1256 (auxin-inhibited endocytosis)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L229-L306>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_032_auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis.lean#L136-L163> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def pin1_membrane_qss_num (k_exo f_j P_tot : Int) : Int := k_exo * f_j * P_tot
def pin1_cytosol_qss_num (k_endo P_tot : Int) : Int := k_endo * P_tot
def pin1_trafficking_partition (k_exo k_endo f1 f2 f3 : Int) : Int := k_endo + k_exo * (f1 + f2 + f3)
theorem jonsson_2006_pin1_trafficking_qss (k_exo k_endo f1 f2 f3 f_j f_k P_tot : Int)
    (hk : k_exo > 0) (hP : P_tot > 0) (hf : f_j > f_k) :
    pin1_cytosol_qss_num k_endo P_tot + pin1_membrane_qss_num k_exo f1 P_tot +
        pin1_membrane_qss_num k_exo f2 P_tot + pin1_membrane_qss_num k_exo f3 P_tot =
      P_tot * pin1_trafficking_partition k_exo k_endo f1 f2 f3 ∧
    k_endo * pin1_membrane_qss_num k_exo f_j P_tot =
      k_exo * f_j * pin1_cytosol_qss_num k_endo P_tot ∧
    pin1_membrane_qss_num k_exo f_j P_tot > pin1_membrane_qss_num k_exo f_k P_tot ∧
    pin1_membrane_qss_num 0 f_j P_tot = 0
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "dP_ij/dt = k_exo f(a_j) P_cyt,i − k_endo P_ij,  P_cyt,i + ∑_j P_ij = P_tot;  P*_ij = k_exo f_j P_tot / Z_i,  P*_cyt = k_endo P_tot / Z_i,  Z_i = k_endo + k_exo ∑_k f_k;  k_endo P*_ij = k_exo f_j P*_cyt;  f_j > f_k ⇒ P*_ij > P*_ik;  k_exo = 0 (BFA) ⇒ P*_ij = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2005.09.052>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/35096571>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03633>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0015>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0154>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.497009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Up-the-Gradient Auxin-PIN1 Polarized Transport & Turing-Like Phyllotactic Spacing" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.pin1_membrane_qss_num" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_032.jonsson_2006_pin1_trafficking_qss" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980/1981) With-the-Flux Canalization Winner-Take-All Law (subepidermal provascular strand; Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Shows that a superlinear flux feedback amplifies any flux asymmetry between competing walls, so a symmetric split is linearly unstable and auxin efflux canalizes into a single-file provascular strand connecting the L1 convergence point to the existing vasculature (Bayer et al. 2009 integration) | Variables: J_1, J_2: net auxin efflux through two competing walls of a subepidermal cell; Φ: with-the-flux exocytosis targeting (quadratic case of Φ = J^n/(K^n + J^n)); α: feedback gain (k_exo P_cyt)" ;
    dct:source "Mitchison GJ (1980) Proc. R. Soc. Lond. B 207:79-109; Mitchison GJ (1981) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. Lond. B 295:461-471; Feugier et al. (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:366-375; Bayer et al. (2009) Genes Dev. 23:373-384" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-jonsson-auxin-pin1-meristem.py#L617-L770>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_032_auxin_pin1_phyllotaxis.lean#L183-L202> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def flux_feedback_quadratic (J : Int) : Int := J * J
theorem mitchison_1980_canalization_winner_take_all (J1 J2 alpha : Int)
    (h2 : J2 ≥ 0) (h : J1 > J2) (ha : alpha > 0) :
    flux_feedback_quadratic J1 - flux_feedback_quadratic J2 = (J1 - J2) * (J1 + J2) ∧
    flux_feedback_quadratic J1 > flux_feedback_quadratic J2 ∧
    alpha * (flux_feedback_quadratic J1 - flux_feedback_quadratic J2) > 0
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Φ(J) = J²;  J_1 > J_2 ≥ 0 ⇒ Φ(J_1) − Φ(J_2) = (J_1 − J_2)(J_1 + J_2) > 0;  α > 0 ⇒ α (Φ(J_1) − Φ(J_2)) > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2005.09.052>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
